<title>USA: SEC bars derivatives dealer after towns' losses.</title>
<headline>SEC bars derivatives dealer after towns' losses.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>An administrative law judge barred dealer Kenneth Schulte from the securities markets because of derivatives sales that led to $8.2 million in losses for 13 cities, counties and school districts in Ohio, the Securities and Exchange Commission said Friday.</p>
<p>Judge Brenda Murray said that from 1990 to 1994, Schulte sold over $39.4 million in interest only securities, inverse floaters and other derivatives to the localities without adequately disclosing risks.</p>
</text>
